<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import SeeTheMessage from './lib/SeeTheMessage.abide'
import seeTheMessage from './lib/SeeTheMessage.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/components/announce', '/components/toasts', '/components/chart']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/reports/lib/WonRevenue.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the same words said twice land twice, each replacing the last'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/announce.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a message with no Announcer standing warns once — 50.36'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Read every announcement out from one place">
        <p>Render <code>Announcer</code> once, in the root layout, and hide it with a class. Its
            two live regions stand empty from the first paint, which is what lets a screen reader
            hear the first message that lands in them.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import Announcer from '@abide/abide/Announcer.abide'
            </script>

            <html lang="en">
                <body>
                    <slot />
                    <Announcer class="sr-only" />
                </body>
            </html>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="See the message while you build">
        <p>Leave the class off to read what a screen reader is told. Each message lands in the
            region its politeness names, the <code>polite</code> and the <code>assertive</code> part,
            and replaces the one before it, so neither grows into a log. A page shows its messages
            in the last <code>Announcer</code> it renders.</p>
        <Example code={seeTheMessage}><SeeTheMessage /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
